@api @get_echo
Feature: GET Echo Endpoint Structure Validation with Multiple Query Parameters # features/test_get_echo_structure.feature:2
  As a QA engineer
  I want to validate the GET /get echo endpoint response structure
  So that I can ensure the response contains required contract keys
  @api @get_echo
  Feature: GET Echo Endpoint Structure Validation with Multiple Query Parameters  # features/test_get_echo_structure.feature:2

  @contract @positive
  Scenario: Verify GET response is a JSON object with required keys  # features/test_get_echo_structure.feature:14
    Given the API base URL is configured                             # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a GET request to "/get" with query parameters:       # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:25
      | key | value |
      | foo | bar   |
      | baz | value |
    Then the response should be a JSON object                        # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:77
    And the response JSON should contain key "args"                  # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:82
    And the response JSON should contain key "headers"               # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:82
    And the response JSON should contain key "url"                   # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:82

@api @get_echo
Feature: GET Echo Endpoint URL Query Parameter Validation # features/test_get_echo_url_params.feature:2
  As a QA engineer
  I want to validate the GET /get echo endpoint URL contains query parameters
  So that I can ensure the API correctly reflects the request URL
  @api @get_echo
  Feature: GET Echo Endpoint URL Query Parameter Validation  # features/test_get_echo_url_params.feature:2

  @contract @positive
  Scenario: Verify GET response URL contains query parameters    # features/test_get_echo_url_params.feature:14
    Given the API base URL is configured                         # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:16
    When I send a GET request to "/get" with query parameters:   # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:25
      | key | value |
      | foo | bar   |
      | baz | value |
    Then the response status code should be 200                  # features/steps/test_response_steps.py:56
    And the JSON key "url" should contain "postman-echo.com/get" # features/steps/test_get_echo_url_params_steps.py:13
    And the JSON key "url" should contain "foo=bar"              # features/steps/test_get_echo_url_params_steps.py:13
    And the JSON key "url" should contain "baz=value"            # features/steps/test_get_echo_url_params_steps.py:13

